<title>UK: SEK sets 20 billion yen dual-currency bond.</title>
<headline>SEK sets 20 billion yen dual-currency bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers New Japan Securities Europe Ltd and IBJ International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SWEDISH EXPORT CREDIT</p>
<p> AMT    20 BLN YEN    COUPON   **5.1 PCT   MATURITY    03.FEB.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    03.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.50	LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> NOTES	**REDEMPTION $4,281.55 PER 500,000 YEN DENOMINATION</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AA3/AA+   DENOMS (M) 500	 SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
